parts.text:
THE TENANT COVENANTS with the Landlord as follows:
(a) to pay the rent on the days and in the manner stated in this agreement;
(b) not to assign, sublet, charge or otherwise part with possession of the Premises or any part of them without the written consent of the Landlord first obtained, such consent not to be unreasonably withheld;
(c) not to make any alteration to the Premises without the written consent of the Landlord, and to restore the Premises to their original state at the end of the tenancy;
(d) to keep the Premises in a good state of repair, fair wear and tear excepted;
(e) to use the Premises for {{use}} purposes only;
(f) to deliver up possession of the Premises at the end of the tenancy.
